  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts with a procedural robot built only from primitives. It passes typecheck. I did not run `vite build` or view the scene in a browser, so the lighting and framing are untested.\n\n- **Robot:** Every joint is a `group` with a mutable runtime id, so rotating a joint swings everything below it. There are 11 joints: hips, chest, neck/head, two shoulders, two elbows, two hips and two knees.\n- **Idle animation:** An `app.onFrame` callback drives the joints each frame. The robot breathes, sways its weight side to side, turns its head slowly and swings its arms and elbows gently. Its knees flex a little with the sway.\n- **Lighting:** The background is near-black. A warm shadow-casting key light shines on a dark floor. There are magenta and cyan rim lights, and the ambient light is dim.\n- **Camera:** A perspective camera sits slightly off-axis, targeting the robot's centre at y=1.0 and sized to fit the full height.\n- **Render contract:** The scene draws into the existing `#app` canvas, and the engine's own loop renders every frame. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set to true in a `requestAnimationFrame` callback after `app.ready()`.\n\n",
